1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,300
Every family has a beginning. Ours
begins at the old walls of Harar.

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:14,215
My great-grandparents came here as
strangers, carrying little more than a

3
00:00:14,215 --> 00:00:14,700
skill.

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:22,600
They were tailors. Stitch by stitch,
they built a life with their hands.

5
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:29,673
Their children became merchants. The
stitches became trade, and the trade

6
00:00:29,673 --> 00:00:31,000
became a living.

7
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:38,900
What they earned, they saved, for the
ones who would come after them.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,300
My mother worked in the market by day,
and carried her schoolbooks with her.

9
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:53,200
At night, when she was tired, she
studied anyway.

10
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,200
And one day, she graduated.

11
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:08,446
Then she worked long hours in an office,
and gave everything she had so that I

12
00:01:08,446 --> 00:01:09,700
could learn.

13
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:15,787
I graduated in software engineering,
with honours. Today, I work on

14
00:01:15,787 --> 00:01:17,600
artificial intelligence.

15
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:27,785
Nothing I have is mine alone. It is the
work of everyone who came before me. Now

16
00:01:27,785 --> 00:01:32,500
it is my turn to take us a little
further.

